; jank_compat_test.bl — ported from ExUnit test/beam_lisp/jank_compat_test.exs
;
; The thesis is unchanged: beam-lisp is "jank's language, BEAM's runtime",
; and every fixture under test/fixtures/jank/ is a verbatim block of jank's
; core.jank with its sha256 in a header. The checksum deftest below locks the
; no-local-edits claim; the behaviour deftests load each slice unmodified into a
; throwaway (ns …) and assert the same values the ExUnit suite did.
;
; PARITY: one deftest per ExUnit `test` (109 of them), one `is` per `assert`,
; plus the byte-for-byte checksum deftest over all 117 accepted fixtures.
;
;
; EXUNIT -> BL PARITY MAP. Every ExUnit `test` maps to one deftest;
; the parenthesised n is that deftest is `is` count (= the ExUnit
; `assert` count for the same test). Nothing is dropped or added:
;   constantly returns its arg regardless of args (2)
;     -> constantly-returns-its-arg-regardless-of-args
;   identity returns its argument (1)
;     -> identity-returns-its-argument
;   complement flips a predicate (3)
;     -> complement-flips-a-predicate
;   fnil patches nil arguments (3)
;     -> fnil-patches-nil-arguments
;   key and val read a map entry (2)
;     -> key-and-val-read-a-map-entry
;   if-not selects the else branch when test is truthy (2)
;     -> if-not-selects-the-else-branch-when-test-is-truthy
;   while loops until its test is falsy (1)
;     -> while-loops-until-its-test-is-falsy
;   comp composes right to left, at every arity (4)
;     -> comp-composes-right-to-left-at-every-arity
;   juxt applies every fn to the same args (1)
;     -> juxt-applies-every-fn-to-the-same-args
;   partial fixes leading arguments (3)
;     -> partial-fixes-leading-arguments
;   some returns the first logical-true result, else nil (2)
;     -> some-returns-the-first-logical-true-result-else-nil
;   not-any? is the complement of some (2)
;     -> not-any-is-the-complement-of-some
;   trampoline runs a thunk-returning loop in constant stack (2)
;     -> trampoline-runs-a-thunk-returning-loop-in-constant-stack
;   -> threads through the first argument position (3)
;     -> threads-through-the-first-argument-position
;   ->> threads through the last argument position (2)
;     -> threads-through-the-last-argument-position
;   if-let binds only when the test is truthy (3)
;     -> if-let-binds-only-when-the-test-is-truthy
;   when-let binds and runs its body only when truthy (2)
;     -> when-let-binds-and-runs-its-body-only-when-truthy
;   dotimes runs its body n times, binding the index (1)
;     -> dotimes-runs-its-body-n-times-binding-the-index
;   doseq walks a collection for side effects (1)
;     -> doseq-walks-a-collection-for-side-effects
;   doto threads a value through side-effecting forms and returns it (1)
;     -> doto-threads-a-value-through-side-effecting-forms-and-returns-it
;   memoize caches by argument list (1)
;     -> memoize-caches-by-argument-list
;   reverse returns the items in reverse order (2)
;     -> reverse-returns-the-items-in-reverse-order
;   run! reduces a proc for side effects and returns nil (1)
;     -> run-reduces-a-proc-for-side-effects-and-returns-nil
;   every-pred combines predicates with and (3)
;     -> every-pred-combines-predicates-with-and
;   some-fn combines predicates with or, returning the first truthy (3)
;     -> some-fn-combines-predicates-with-or-returning-the-first-truthy
;   if-some binds only when the test is non-nil (3)
;     -> if-some-binds-only-when-the-test-is-non-nil
;   when-some runs its body only when the test is non-nil (2)
;     -> when-some-runs-its-body-only-when-the-test-is-non-nil
;   repeatedly builds a lazy sequence of thunk calls (1)
;     -> repeatedly-builds-a-lazy-sequence-of-thunk-calls
;   take-while takes the prefix while pred holds (coll arity) (1)
;     -> take-while-takes-the-prefix-while-pred-holds-coll-arity
;   drop-while drops the prefix while pred holds (coll arity) (1)
;     -> drop-while-drops-the-prefix-while-pred-holds-coll-arity
;   split-at returns a vector of take and drop (1)
;     -> split-at-returns-a-vector-of-take-and-drop
;   interleave merges colls positionally (2-arity docstring example) (1)
;     -> interleave-merges-colls-positionally-2-arity-docstring-example
;   update applies f to a key's value (3)
;     -> update-applies-f-to-a-key-s-value
;   mapcat concatenates the mapped results (coll arity) (1)
;     -> mapcat-concatenates-the-mapped-results-coll-arity
;   remove filters out the items pred accepts (1)
;     -> remove-filters-out-the-items-pred-accepts
;   assoc-in sets a value at a nested path (2)
;     -> assoc-in-sets-a-value-at-a-nested-path
;   update-in applies a fn at a nested path (1)
;     -> update-in-applies-a-fn-at-a-nested-path
;   partition splits into non-overlapping groups (3)
;     -> partition-splits-into-non-overlapping-groups
;   cond-> threads only through the forms whose test is true (3)
;     -> cond-threads-only-through-the-forms-whose-test-is-true
;   cond->> threads through the last argument position (1)
;     -> cond-threads-through-the-last-argument-position
;   as-> binds the threaded value to a name (1)
;     -> as-binds-the-threaded-value-to-a-name
;   some-> and some->> stop at the first nil (4)
;     -> some-and-some-stop-at-the-first-nil
;   assert passes silently and throws on a false test (2)
;     -> assert-passes-silently-and-throws-on-a-false-test
;   keys and vals walk the map through a transient (3)
;     -> keys-and-vals-walk-the-map-through-a-transient
;   zipmap, frequencies and group-by build maps with transients (3)
;     -> zipmap-frequencies-and-group-by-build-maps-with-transients
;   max-key returns the x with the greatest (k x) (1)
;     -> max-key-returns-the-x-with-the-greatest-k-x
;   min-key returns the x with the least (k x) (1)
;     -> min-key-returns-the-x-with-the-least-k-x
;   condp dispatches through a binary predicate (4)
;     -> condp-dispatches-through-a-binary-predicate
;   set builds a set through a transient and a set literal (2)
;     -> set-builds-a-set-through-a-transient-and-a-set-literal
;   distinct drops duplicates, keeping first-seen order (1)
;     -> distinct-drops-duplicates-keeping-first-seen-order
;   select-keys narrows a map (2)
;     -> select-keys-narrows-a-map
;   name, namespace and keyword run on the cpp/* primitive shim (4)
;     -> name-namespace-and-keyword-run-on-the-cpp-primitive-shim
;   merge-with combines colliding keys through a fn (1)
;     -> merge-with-combines-colliding-keys-through-a-fn
;   sort-by orders by a key fn (1)
;     -> sort-by-orders-by-a-key-fn
;   flatten walks arbitrarily nested sequentials (1)
;     -> flatten-walks-arbitrarily-nested-sequentials
;   interleave and lazy-cat handle a lazy-seq over a bare collection (4)
;     -> interleave-and-lazy-cat-handle-a-lazy-seq-over-a-bare-collection
;   for comprehends, nests, and stays lazy (4)
;     -> for-comprehends-nests-and-stays-lazy
;   completing adds the arity-1 and arity-0 signatures to a reducing fn (3)
;     -> completing-adds-the-arity-1-and-arity-0-signatures-to-a-reducing-fn
;   reduce folds with no init, and the [f init coll] arity now via the cpp shim (4)
;     -> reduce-folds-with-no-init-and-the-f-init-coll-arity-now-via-the-cpp-shim
;   not= negates = at every arity (3)
;     -> not-negates-at-every-arity
;   pos-int? tests a positive fixed-precision integer (3)
;     -> pos-int-tests-a-positive-fixed-precision-integer
;   nthnext returns the nth seq or nil (3)
;     -> nthnext-returns-the-nth-seq-or-nil
;   nthrest returns the nth rest or empty (3)
;     -> nthrest-returns-the-nth-rest-or-empty
;   take-nth keeps every nth item (coll + transducer arity; rem now core) (3)
;     -> take-nth-keeps-every-nth-item-coll-transducer-arity-rem-now-core
;   map applies f across one or more colls (vendored upstream arities) (2)
;     -> map-applies-f-across-one-or-more-colls-vendored-upstream-arities
;   map-indexed threads the index (coll arity; transducer needs volatile!) (1)
;     -> map-indexed-threads-the-index-coll-arity-transducer-needs-volatile
;   keep drops nil results (1)
;     -> keep-drops-nil-results
;   keep-indexed drops nil results, threading the index (1)
;     -> keep-indexed-drops-nil-results-threading-the-index
;   split-with partitions by a predicate (needs upstream juxt) (2)
;     -> split-with-partitions-by-a-predicate-needs-upstream-juxt
;   dorun forces a seq for side effects and returns nil (2)
;     -> dorun-forces-a-seq-for-side-effects-and-returns-nil
;   doall forces a seq and returns it (needs upstream dorun) (2)
;     -> doall-forces-a-seq-and-returns-it-needs-upstream-dorun
;   take-last returns the last n items (1)
;     -> take-last-returns-the-last-n-items
;   mapv returns a vector (all arities, into + multi-coll map ship) (3)
;     -> mapv-returns-a-vector-all-arities-into-multi-coll-map-ship
;   filterv returns a vector of the kept items (2)
;     -> filterv-returns-a-vector-of-the-kept-items
;   distinct? is true when no two args are equal (4)
;     -> distinct-is-true-when-no-two-args-are-equal
;   filter keeps the items pred accepts (vendored coll arity) (2)
;     -> filter-keeps-the-items-pred-accepts-vendored-coll-arity
;   dedupe removes consecutive duplicates (needs upstream when-some) (2)
;     -> dedupe-removes-consecutive-duplicates-needs-upstream-when-some
;   nfirst is (next (first x)) (2)
;     -> nfirst-is-next-first-x
;   fnext is (first (next x)) (2)
;     -> fnext-is-first-next-x
;   map-entry? tests a 2-element vector (3)
;     -> map-entry-tests-a-2-element-vector
;   not-every? is the negation of every? (2)
;     -> not-every-is-the-negation-of-every
;   replicate builds n copies (deprecated alias of take+repeat) (1)
;     -> replicate-builds-n-copies-deprecated-alias-of-take-repeat
;   comparator turns a binary pred into a -1/0/1 comparator (3)
;     -> comparator-turns-a-binary-pred-into-a-1-0-1-comparator
;   list? via ^{:arglists …} metadata and the is_list shim (2)
;     -> list-via-arglists-metadata-and-the-is-list-shim
;   reduced wraps a value for early reduction termination (1)
;     -> reduced-wraps-a-value-for-early-reduction-termination
;   reduced? tests the reduced wrapper (2)
;     -> reduced-tests-the-reduced-wrapper
;   ensure-reduced returns its arg if reduced, else wraps it (3)
;     -> ensure-reduced-returns-its-arg-if-reduced-else-wraps-it
;   unreduced unwraps a reduced, passes others through (2)
;     -> unreduced-unwraps-a-reduced-passes-others-through
;   transduce reduces with a transformed reducing fn (2)
;     -> transduce-reduces-with-a-transformed-reducing-fn
;   preserving-reduced re-wraps a reduced result (2)
;     -> preserving-reduced-re-wraps-a-reduced-result
;   cat concatenates each input collection into the reduction (1)
;     -> cat-concatenates-each-input-collection-into-the-reduction
;   peek reads a vector's last or a list's first, nil when empty (3)
;     -> peek-reads-a-vector-s-last-or-a-list-s-first-nil-when-empty
;   pop removes a vector's last or a list's first (2)
;     -> pop-removes-a-vector-s-last-or-a-list-s-first
;   volatile! with vreset! and vswap! builds a mutable cell (2)
;     -> volatile-with-vreset-and-vswap-builds-a-mutable-cell
;   inc' promotes past the fixed-precision boundary (1)
;     -> inc-promotes-past-the-fixed-precision-boundary
;   int? tests a fixed-precision integer (is_integer shim) (2)
;     -> int-tests-a-fixed-precision-integer-is-integer-shim
;   drop-last returns all but the last n (needs the vendored multi-coll map) (2)
;     -> drop-last-returns-all-but-the-last-n-needs-the-vendored-multi-coll-map
;   interpose separates elements with sep (needs upstream interleave) (2)
;     -> interpose-separates-elements-with-sep-needs-upstream-interleave
;   reductions yields the intermediate values of a reduction (2)
;     -> reductions-yields-the-intermediate-values-of-a-reduction
;   into pours a collection into another, with or without a transducer (8)
;     -> into-pours-a-collection-into-another-with-or-without-a-transducer
;   ratio?, decimal? and sorted? are always false on the BEAM (3)
;     -> ratio-decimal-and-sorted-are-always-false-on-the-beam
;   NaN? is always false because beam-lisp cannot produce a NaN (2)
;     -> nan-is-always-false-because-beam-lisp-cannot-produce-a-nan
;   transducer 1-arities reduce correctly with a completing rf (6)
;     -> transducer-1-arities-reduce-correctly-with-a-completing-rf
;   bit-not is the two's-complement complement (3)
;     -> bit-not-is-the-two-s-complement-complement
;   mod truncates toward negative infinity, matching rem's sign (3)
;     -> mod-truncates-toward-negative-infinity-matching-rem-s-sign
;   double? tests a floating-point value via float? (3)
;     -> double-tests-a-floating-point-value-via-float
;   splitv-at returns a vector of an into-take vector and the drop (2)
;     -> splitv-at-returns-a-vector-of-an-into-take-vector-and-the-drop
;   update-vals maps f over the values, preserving keys and meta (2)
;     -> update-vals-maps-f-over-the-values-preserving-keys-and-meta
;   update-keys maps f over the keys, preserving values (2)
;     -> update-keys-maps-f-over-the-keys-preserving-values
;
; The ExUnit checksum test (1 `assert` over 117 fixtures) ->
;   vendored-slices-are-byte-for-byte-upstream (117 assertions).
;   ExUnit totals: 109 tests + 1 checksum, 240 asserts + 1 checksum
;   = 357 executed assertions. BL totals: 110 deftests, 357 `is` passes.
; Run: bin/bl test test/bl/jank_compat_test.bl

